{title: 137 - We Three Kings}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #137 • KINGS OF ORIENT • 7.8.8.6}
{lyricist: John H. Hopkins}
{composer: John H. Hopkins}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 137}
{meta: tune KINGS OF ORIENT}
{meta: meter 7.8.8.6}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]We three kings of Orient are;
[Em]Bearing [Bm]gifts we traverse afar
[Em]Field and fountain, moor and [Bm]mountain,
[Bm]Following [Em]yonder star.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Em]O star of wonder, [D]star of [G]night,
[G]Star with royal [Am]beauty [G]bright,
[Am]Westward leading, [Em/B]still proceeding,
[D]Guide us to Thy perfect light.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Em]Born a King on Bethlehem's plain,
[Em]Gold I [Bm]bring to crown Him again,
[Em]King forever, ceasing [Bm]never
[Bm]Over us [Em]all to reign.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Em]Frankincense to offer have I;
[Em]Incense [Bm]owns a Deity [Em]nigh;
[Em]Prayer and praising all men [Bm]raising,
[Bm]Worship Him, [Em]God on high.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Em]Myrrh is mine; its bitter perfume
[Em]Breathes [Bm]a life of gathering [Em]gloom:
[Em]Sorrowing, sighing, bleeding, [Bm]dying,
[Bm]Sealed in the stonecold [Em]tomb.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Em]Glorious now behold Him arise,
[Em]King and [Bm]God and sacrifice;
[Em]Alleluia, Alleluia!
[Bm]Sounds through the [Em]earth and skies.
{end_of_verse}
